# Refactor to LangChain, LangGraph, & Pydantic Implementation Plan

This plan details the transition of the offline auditing pipeline to LangChain and LangGraph, using ChatOllama and Pydantic validation. The architecture runs completely offline on local CPU resources (Qwen2.5:7B) while preserving your custom retrieval and Jaccard deduplication logic.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Circular Dependency Prevention**: Because `_retrieve_rag_context` is currently defined inside [app.py](file:///c:/Users/HP/Desktop/New%20folder%20%282%29/src/ui/app.py) (which imports database models and UI states), importing it directly into a standalone `src/ai/audit_graph.py` would cause circular imports. We will import `_retrieve_rag_context` dynamically (lazy import) inside the graph's `retrieve_node` execution or pass it as an input function/handler to keep components clean.

> [!WARNING]
> **CPU Latency & Batching**: Running Qwen2.5:7B on CPU only (16GB RAM) means parallel execution must be bounded to avoid freezing the system. We will preserve your current batch size controls (e.g. 5 controls per batch) and map them to parallel thread execution in Python (`ThreadPoolExecutor`), utilizing LangChain's native async/threading invocation.

