#### [NEW] [audit_models.py](file:///c:/Users/HP/Desktop/New%20folder%20%282%29/src/ai/audit_models.py)
Define the Pydantic schema for the structured LLM output:
- Create `AuditFinding` model matching all target fields and `Literal` restrictions (`status`, `severity`, `evidence_state`).
- Add root validator rules ensuring audit logic conformity:
  - If `status == "COMPLIANT"`, then `severity == "NONE"`, `gap == ""`, and `recommendation == ""`.
  - If `status` is `"PARTIAL"`, then `severity` must be `"LOW"` or `"MEDIUM"`, and evidence, gap, and recommendation must be present.
  - If `status` is `"NON_COMPLIANT"`, then `severity` is any non-none value, and gap/recommendation are required.

